<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Metair yr share dips, div unchanged.</title>
<headline>Metair yr share dips, div unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     744	   vs   784</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 200	   vs   200</p>
<p>    Net income		42.15	 vs   44.39</p>
<p>    Net income after tax  42.15	 vs   45.89</p>
<p>    Turnover		 887.03	 vs  834.30</p>
<p>Full name: Metair Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Metair forecast little growth in new vehicle sales in 1997. It said imports will continue to grow and exports of built up vehicles should also increase. Strategic alliances were also being explored to expand the group's access to markets outside southern Africa but the resulting impact is unlikely to be felt before 1998.</p>
<p>The directors cautioned that Metair was at a preliminary stage of investigating the potential of a possible transaction and pending a further announcement, shareholders were being advised to exercise caution when dealing in their Metair shares.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
